    "id": "shm-mcq-106",
    "questionNumber": 106,
    "question": "Two simple harmonic motions are given by $x_1 = A \\sin(\\omega t)$ and $x_2 = A \\sin(\\omega t + \\delta)$. The resultant motion is along the same line. The amplitude of the resultant motion is $\\sqrt{3} A$. What is the phase difference $\\delta$?",
